  <title>Floor plan area tool | Oz Timber Floor</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Estimate floor area by setting a scale on your own plan and tracing the rooms you want to include in an Oz Timber Floor enquiry.">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="./operon-base.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="./operon-page.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="./port-inline-layout.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="./port-accessibility.css">
  <script type="module" src="./operon-runtime.mjs"></script>
</head><body><a class="port-skip" href="#measurementTool">Skip to measurement tool</a><header class="site-header">
    <div class="shell nav">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Oz Timber Floor home">
        <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>Oz Timber Floor</span>
      </a>
      <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a data-quote-return-link href="/contact/?enquiry=supply-install&amp;source=floor-plan">Quote</a>
        <a href="/products/">Flooring Products</a>
        <a href="/floor-plan/">Floor Plan</a>
        <a href="/guides/">Guides</a>
      </nav>
      <button class="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false">
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
      </button>
      <div class="header-actions">
        <a class="header-phone" href="/contact/" data-track-cta="header_contact_click">Contact</a>
        <a class="button header-quote-button" data-quote-return-link href="/contact/?enquiry=supply-install&amp;source=floor-plan">Request Quote</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero" id="floorplanHero">
      <div class="shell hero-grid">
        <article class="hero-card">
          <span class="eyebrow">Floor Plan Measurement Assistant</span>
          <div class="hero-content-row">
            <div class="hero-copy-block">
              <h1>Measure your flooring area from a floor plan.</h1>
              <p>Upload a floor plan, trace the rooms and send a starting area into your quote.</p>
              <div class="hero-actions oz-source-style-0">
                <a class="button" href="#measurementTool">Start measuring</a>
                <a class="button-secondary" data-quote-return-link href="/contact/?enquiry=supply-install&amp;source=floor-plan">Ask for plan review</a>
              </div>
              <p class="helper oz-source-style-1">Starting area only. Product and final scope are confirmed before booking.</p>
            </div>

            <aside class="hero-mini-panel" aria-label="Measurement summary">
              <strong>Upload, scale, trace, review, quote</strong>
              <ul class="hero-mini-steps">
                <li><span>1</span> Upload the floor plan</li>
                <li><span>2</span> Set scale from a known wall</li>
                <li><span>3</span> Trace flooring rooms</li>
                <li><span>4</span> Review selected area</li>
                <li><span>5</span> Use area in quote</li>
              </ul>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section oz-source-style-2" id="floorplanEntrySection">
      <div class="shell">
        <article class="section-card">
          <span class="eyebrow">Choose measurement path</span>
          <h2 class="oz-source-style-3">Not sure your flooring area?</h2>
          <p>Use the floor plan yourself if you want a measured starting area, or start a quote with area uncertainty if you would rather have the plan reviewed during follow-up.</p>
          <div class="link-grid oz-source-style-4">
            <a class="link-card" href="#measurementTool" data-track-cta="floorplan_self_measure_click">
              <strong>I want to measure it myself</strong>
              <span>Upload, set scale, trace rooms and send the measured area into the quote.</span>
            </a>
            <a class="link-card" data-quote-return-link href="/contact/?enquiry=supply-install&amp;source=floor-plan" data-track-cta="floorplan_review_request_click">
              <strong>I want Oz Timber Floor to review the plan</strong>
              <span>Start the quote with area uncertainty and note that a floor plan needs review.</span>
            </a>
            <a class="link-card" href="/guides/" data-track-cta="floorplan_measurement_guide_click">
              <strong>Read the measurement guide</strong>
              <span>Understand what to include before tracing or sending an area into the quote.</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="floorplanGuideSection" class="oz-source-style-5">
      <div class="shell">
        <article class="section-card">
          <span class="eyebrow">How To Use It</span>
          <h2 class="oz-source-style-3">How the measurement tool works</h2>
          <div class="step-grid">
            <div class="step-card">
              <strong>1. Upload floor plan</strong>
              <span>Use a PDF, JPG or PNG.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="step-card">
              <strong>2. Set scale</strong>
              <span>Click two points on a known wall, then enter the real distance.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="step-card">
              <strong>3. Trace room</strong>
              <span>Trace the flooring rooms and close each shape near the start point.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="step-card">
              <strong>4. Use area in quote</strong>
              <span>Send measured area into the quote. Product and final scope are confirmed separately.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section oz-source-style-2" id="floorplanTrustSection">
      <div class="shell">
        <article class="section-card">
          <span class="eyebrow">Scope clarity</span>
          <h2 class="oz-source-style-3">Clear scope before the job is booked</h2>
          <p>Floor plan area is one part of a flooring quote. Product, removal, disposal, trims and stairs are reviewed before final confirmation.</p>
          <div class="trust-card-grid oz-source-style-4">
            <article class="trust-card">
              <h3>Area checked</h3>
              <p>Use the plan to create a starting area, then keep final measurement open for review.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card">
              <h3>Rooms included clearly</h3>
              <p>Only trace rooms receiving flooring so the quote does not include the wrong spaces.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card">
              <h3>Site scope still reviewed</h3>
              <p>Removal, floor preparation, stairs and trims are confirmed separately.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="trust-card">
              <h3>Quote handoff ready</h3>
              <p>Measured area can be carried into the quote without changing product or pricing logic.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tool-section" id="measurementTool">
      <div class="shell layout">
        <article class="section-card workspace-card">
          <div class="tool-header">
            <span class="eyebrow">Measurement Tool</span>
            <h2>Upload, set scale and trace rooms</h2>
            <p>Trace Room Mode measures real flooring area from your plan. Product and installation scope are reviewed separately.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="status hidden oz-source-style-6" id="resumeMeasurementBanner">
            <strong class="oz-source-style-7">Previous floor plan measurement found.</strong>
            <span>Resume your measured rooms. For privacy, choose the same plan file again to reconnect its measured rooms.</span>
            <div class="action-row oz-source-style-1">
              <button class="button-secondary" id="resumeMeasurementButton" type="button">Resume measurement</button>
              <button class="button-quiet" id="startNewMeasurementButton" type="button">Start new</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="workspace-main">
            <div class="tool-panel-shell">
              <div class="tool-subsection">
                <div class="tool-subsection-header">
                    <h3 class="tool-subsection-title">1. Upload floor plan</h3>
                    <p class="helper oz-source-style-8">Use a PDF, JPG or PNG. A plan with room walls and one known dimension gives the best result.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="field upload-field oz-source-style-9">
                  <label for="planUpload">Choose plan file</label>
                  <input id="planUpload" disabled type="file" accept="image/*,.pdf,application/pdf">
                </div>
                <div class="status" id="uploadStatus">Upload a PDF, JPG or PNG floor plan to start measuring.</div>
                <div class="tool-button-row compact hidden" id="planFileActions">
                  <button class="button-danger" id="clearPlanButton" type="button">Clear floor plan</button>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="mode-row quick-room-hidden" aria-hidden="true">
                <button class="mode-chip active" type="button" data-mode="trace">
                  <strong>Trace Room Mode</strong>
                  <span>Trace rooms receiving flooring.</span>
                </button>
                <button class="mode-chip" type="button" data-mode="quick">
                  <strong>Quick Room Mode</strong>
                  <span>Click inside a room and review the suggested outline.</span>
                </button>
              </div>

              <div class="mode-panel active hidden" id="tracePanel">
                <div class="tool-subsection">
                  <div class="tool-subsection-header">
                    <h3 class="tool-subsection-title">2. Set scale and trace</h3>
                    <p class="helper oz-source-style-8">Use the longest labelled wall dimension available for best results.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="tool-button-row compact">
                    <button class="button-secondary" id="setScaleButton" type="button">Step 1. Set scale</button>
                    <button class="button-secondary" id="resetScaleButton" type="button">Reset scale</button>
                    <button class="button-quiet" id="verifyScaleButton" type="button">Verify scale with another wall</button>
                  </div>

                  <div class="summary-box oz-source-style-10" id="scaleDetailsPanel">
                    <strong>Scale status: <span id="scaleStatusLabel">Not set</span></strong>
                    <div class="scale-detail-grid oz-source-style-11">
                      <div><span>Known distance</span><strong id="scaleKnownDistance">-</strong></div>
                      <div><span>Pixel distance</span><strong id="scalePixelDistance">-</strong></div>
                      <div><span>Pixels per metre</span><strong id="scalePixelsPerMetre">-</strong></div>
                      <div><span>Metres per pixel</span><strong id="scaleMetresPerPixel">-</strong></div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="helper oz-source-style-12" id="scaleQualityMessage">Set scale before tracing rooms.</p>
                  </div>

                  <div class="tool-button-row oz-source-style-13">
                    <button class="button-secondary" id="startTraceButton" type="button">Step 2. Trace room</button>
                    <button class="button-quiet" id="undoTracePointButton" type="button">Undo point</button>
                    <button class="button-quiet" id="clearTraceButton" type="button">Clear trace</button>
                    <button class="button-secondary" id="finishTraceButton" type="button">Finish room</button>
                  </div>

                  <div class="summary-box oz-source-style-10">
                    <strong>Trace rooms</strong>
                    <p class="helper oz-source-style-14">Click each corner of the flooring area. Close the room by clicking near the first point, or use Finish room.</p>
                    <div class="trace-detail-grid">
                      <div><span>Current points</span><strong id="tracePointCount">0</strong></div>
                      <div><span>Shape status</span><strong id="traceShapeStatus">Open</strong></div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="trace-warning oz-source-style-12" id="traceValidationMessage"></p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="mode-panel quick-room-hidden" id="quickPanel" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="tool-subsection">
                  <div class="tool-subsection-header">
                    <h3 class="tool-subsection-title">2. Quick Room Mode</h3>
                    <p class="helper oz-source-style-8">Click inside a room and Oz Timber Floor will suggest the likely flooring area. Review the outline before adding it to your measured area.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="status">
                    Suggested areas are a starting point only. Accepted totals use the reviewed outline; check its boundaries before sharing an area estimate.
                  </div>
                  <div class="action-row">
                    <button class="button" id="suggestAllAreasButton" type="button">Suggest areas</button>
                    <button class="button-secondary" id="prepareQuickModeButton" type="button">Prepare Quick Room Mode</button>
                    <button class="button-secondary" id="quickModeInfoButton" type="button">Use Manual Trace</button>
                  </div>
                  <p class="helper oz-source-style-12">Review suggested areas before using them in your quote.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="quick-status-grid" aria-live="polite">
                  <div class="quick-status-card">
                    <strong>Uploaded plan</strong>
                    <span id="quickImageLoadedLabel">No</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="quick-status-card">
                    <strong>Scale set</strong>
                    <span id="quickScaleStatusLabel">No</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="quick-status-card">
                    <strong>Suggestion status</strong>
                    <span id="quickDetectionStatusLabel">Not started</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="quick-status-card">
                    <strong>Saved quick rooms</strong>
                    <span id="quickSuggestedCountLabel">0</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="quick-status-card">
                    <strong>Selected total area</strong>
                    <span id="quickSelectedTotalLabel">0.00 m²</span>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="quick-suggestion-card hidden" id="quickSuggestionPanel" data-confidence="">
                  <div>
                    <strong id="quickSuggestionTitle">Suggested room</strong>
                    <p class="helper oz-source-style-15" id="quickSuggestionCopy">Review the outline on the plan before adding it.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="quick-suggestion-meta">
                    <span class="pill" id="quickSuggestionArea">0.00 m²</span>
                    <span class="pill" id="quickSuggestionConfidence">Confidence</span>
                  </div>
                  <ul class="quick-reason-list" id="quickSuggestionReasons"></ul>
                  <div class="action-row">
                    <button class="button" id="acceptQuickRoomButton" type="button">Accept room</button>
                    <button class="button-secondary" id="editQuickRoomButton" type="button">Edit manually</button>
                    <button class="button-quiet" id="discardQuickRoomButton" type="button">Discard</button>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <canvas id="quickPreviewCanvas" width="1200" height="860" class="hidden"></canvas>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="workspace-stage">
              <div class="status" id="traceStatus">
                Upload a floor plan, set scale, then trace rooms receiving flooring.
              </div>
              <div class="status" id="canvasStatus">Upload a floor plan to begin.</div>
              <div class="canvas-shell hidden" id="canvasShell">
                <div class="canvas-stage">
                  <canvas tabindex="0" aria-label="Floor plan drawing. Use the keyboard point controls below as an alternative to clicking." id="planCanvas" width="1200" height="860"></canvas>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <aside class="summary-card workspace-summary">
          <div class="summary-heading">
            <span class="eyebrow">Selected Area</span>
            <h3 class="oz-source-style-16">Selected flooring area</h3>
            <p>Select only the rooms where flooring will be installed, then send the total back into your quote.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="summary-box">
            <strong>Total selected flooring area</strong>
            <div class="summary-total" id="selectedAreaTotal">0.00 m²</div>
            <div id="roomsCountText">0 measured rooms</div>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-grid">
            <div class="metric">
              <strong id="scaleReadout">Not set</strong>
              <span class="helper">Current scale</span>
            </div>
            <div class="metric">
              <strong id="flooringCount">0</strong>
              <span class="helper">Included rooms</span>
            </div>
            <div class="metric">
              <strong id="excludedCount">0</strong>
              <span class="helper">Excluded rooms</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="summary-box">
            <div class="oz-source-style-17">
              <strong>Measurement confidence</strong>
              <span class="pill warn" id="measurementConfidenceTag">Low</span>
            </div>
            <p class="helper oz-source-style-18" id="measurementConfidenceText">Upload a plan, set scale and trace rooms before using the area in quote.</p>
            <div class="confidence-checklist oz-source-style-11" id="confidenceChecklist"></div>
            <p class="helper oz-source-style-15" id="scaleWarningText"></p>
          </div>

          <details class="summary-box room-list-panel" open>
            <summary>
              <strong>Measured rooms</strong>
              <span class="helper">Open room list</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="rooms-table" id="roomsTable"></div>
          </details>

          <div class="summary-box">
            <strong>Review before quote</strong>
            <p class="helper oz-source-style-18">Only include rooms where flooring will be installed.</p>
            <p class="helper oz-source-style-19">Common areas to exclude:</p>
            <ul class="helper oz-source-style-20">
              <li>Bathrooms</li>
              <li>Balconies</li>
              <li>Garage</li>
              <li>Outdoor areas</li>
              <li>Voids</li>
              <li>Rooms not receiving flooring</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="summary-box">
            <strong>Ready to continue your quote?</strong>
            <p class="helper oz-source-style-18">Send the selected floor area back to the quote form, then confirm product and final scope before submitting.</p>
            <div class="summary-actions oz-source-style-21">
              <button class="button" id="useAreaInQuoteButton" type="button">Use selected measured area in quote</button>
              <button class="button-danger" id="clearRoomsButton" type="button">Clear rooms</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="floorplanFaq">
      <div class="shell">
        <article class="section-card">
          <span class="eyebrow">Floor Plan Measurement FAQ</span>
          <h2 class="oz-source-style-3">Before you use the measured area</h2>
          <div class="rooms-table">
            <details class="summary-box">
              <summary><strong>Is this the final flooring measurement?</strong></summary>
              <p class="helper oz-source-style-18">No. It gives a measured starting area from your floor plan. Final details can still be confirmed before installation.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="summary-box">
              <summary><strong>What kind of floor plan works best?</strong></summary>
              <p class="helper oz-source-style-18">A PDF, JPG or PNG with visible room walls and at least one known dimension.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="summary-box">
              <summary><strong>Does this calculate the final quote?</strong></summary>
              <p class="helper oz-source-style-18">No. It sends measured area into the quote. Product choice, main inclusions and final project details are reviewed separately.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="summary-box">
              <summary><strong>Should I include every room?</strong></summary>
              <p class="helper oz-source-style-18">Only trace rooms where flooring will be installed.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="floorplanPlanningLinksTitle">
      <div class="shell">
        <article class="section-card">
          <span class="eyebrow">Plan the full quote</span>
          <h2 id="floorplanPlanningLinksTitle" class="oz-source-style-3">Use the measured area with the right project context</h2>
          <p>A floor plan creates a starting area. Product suitability, apartment requirements and the written installation scope still need separate review.</p>
          <div class="link-grid oz-source-style-4">
            <a class="link-card" href="/engineered-timber-flooring/"><strong>Planning apartment flooring?</strong><span>Check access, building requirements, acoustic questions and removal scope.</span></a>
            <a class="link-card" href="/products/"><strong>Choose a flooring direction</strong><span>Compare hybrid, laminate and engineered timber before quoting.</span></a>
            <a class="link-card" href="/contact/?enquiry=service&amp;source=floor-plan-review"><strong>Need help reviewing your plan?</strong><span>Ask the Oz team which measurements and project details to confirm.</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

